const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why does my ice machine make less ice at events than at the commissary?",
    a: "Heat and power. Ice production ratings are measured at mild air and water temperatures, and a closed truck on a summer afternoon is anything but mild, so an air-cooled machine makes less ice per cycle and runs longer. Add a generator that sags when the compressor starts and a condenser coated in fryer grease, and output drops again. We measure all three before touching refrigeration parts."
  },
  {
    q: "Why are the cubes thin, or only forming on one side?",
    a: "On a truck, two causes lead the list. Water: a weak onboard pump, a low fresh water tank, air in the line or a clogged filter keeps the machine from filling fully. Level: cube machines need to sit level so water runs evenly over the evaporator, and a truck parked on a crowned street tilts it. We check pressure during fill and the level of the unit as parked."
  },
  {
    q: "How often should a food truck ice machine be cleaned?",
    a: "Follow the manufacturer's cleaning and sanitizing schedule as the minimum, and expect a truck to need it more often than a restaurant machine, because heat, grease and hard commissary water build scale and slime faster. Ice is food, so a dirty machine is a health problem before it's a production problem."
  },
  {
    q: "Can a weak water pump really stop an ice machine?",
    a: "Yes. Every cycle expects enough water in a set amount of time. A tired 12-volt pump or a nearly empty tank leaves the machine short, which shows up as partial cubes, long cycles or a water fault. It's one of the first things we test on a truck, because it's cheaper to fix than anything inside the machine."
  },
  {
    q: "What does the diagnostic cost, and how soon can you come?",
    a: "The diagnostic is $120 and it's waived when you approve the repair. Same-day service is available across Los Angeles, usually at your commissary, with phones answered 24/7. Cleaning, descaling and parts are quoted in writing after we look at the machine."
  }
];

